+                      dirs: Mapping[str, Path]) -> set[str]:
+    """At the end of the run, name each published PR that holds a commit a member's branch
+    lost, by ``rewrites`` (:func:`_note_base_rewrites`): the refusals made since the run's
+    last fold (#738). A refusal names every PR of the run that already held such a commit,
+    but it is made before the wave's other bundles are pointed and built. One of them cut
+    from the run's line, which still holds the head the line took, or built on a base of
+    its own built before the refusal in the same wave, holds such a head too. Only a bundle
+    that pushed a branch this run has a PR (``taken``, :func:`_heads_taken`): one closed
+    with no patch, or whose publish pushed nothing, is never named. A head is judged lost
+    as the refusal judged it; no fold has checked that branch since (one that did, and went
+    on, found it mended: the caller clears ``rewrites``). Each PR the refusal did not name
+    already is named on one stderr line (``dirs``: bundle name → its directory), with the
+    fix. Returns the members whose lost head a PR holds, those the refusal named included:
+    like a late rewrite (#695), they fail the run."""
+    bases, line_prs = taken
+    failed: set[str] = set()
+    for m, (ref, lost, by, named) in sorted(rewrites.items()):
+        on = [(o, h, f"is cut from {publish.read_stack_base(dirs[o])} at "
+                     f"{publish.read_stack_base_tip(dirs[o])[:12]}")
+              for o, h in line_prs.get(m, ()) if h in lost]
+        on += [(o, heads[m], f"is built on its own base {branch}")
